{"name":"The Fang","hex":"#585673","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fang","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, pointed canine tooth used for biting and tearing flesh. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Synonym of mandible, the long mouthpart of insects and other invertebrates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike or attack with the fangs.","To enable to catch or tear; to furnish with fangs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fang"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Fang (frozen waterfall)","blocks":[{"text":"The Fang is a 165 foot tall waterfall in Eagle County near the town of Vail, Colorado. It lies in what is called the \"Rigid Designator Amphitheatre\", which is a significant location in North America for ice climbing and mixed climbing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/The_Fang_%28icefall%29.jpg/330px-The_Fang_%28icefall%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fang_(frozen_waterfall)"},{"title":"Mount Erebus","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Erebus is the southernmost active volcano on Earth, located on Ross Island in the Ross Dependency in Antarctica. With a summit elevation of 3,792 metres (12,441 ft), it is the second most prominent mountain in Antarctica and the second-highest volcano in Antarctica. It is the highest point on Ross Island, which is also home to three inactive volcanoes: Mount Terror, Mount Bird, and Mount Terra Nova. It makes Ross Island the sixth-highest island on Earth by highest point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Mt_erebus.jpg/330px-Mt_erebus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Erebus"},{"title":"Fang","blocks":[{"text":"A fang is a long, pointed tooth. In mammals, a fang is a modified maxillary tooth, used for biting and tearing flesh. In snakes, it is a specialized tooth that is associated with a venom gland. Spiders also have external fangs, which are part of the chelicerae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg/330px-Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fang"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Anorthoclase-219058.jpg/330px-Anorthoclase-219058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Anorthoclase-219058.jpg/330px-Anorthoclase-219058.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Anorthoclase crystal (45 mm long) from Mount Erebus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnorthoclase-219058.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Mount_Erebus.png/500px-Mount_Erebus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Mount_Erebus.png/1280px-Mount_Erebus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Mount_Erebus.png/500px-Mount_Erebus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of Mount Erebus (and Adélie penguins) taken by the Terra Nova expedition in 1913","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Erebus.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mount_Erebus_craters%2C_Ross_Island%2C_Antarctica_%28aerial_view%2C_18_December_2000%29.jpg/500px-Mount_Erebus_craters%2C_Ross_Island%2C_Antarctica_%28aerial_view%2C_18_December_2000%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Mount_Erebus_craters%2C_Ross